            "kind": "REWORK",
            "comments": [
                {
                    "file": "yaml/xyz/openbmc_project/Logging/Manager.interface.yaml",
                    "line": 3,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Deepak Kodihalli",
                        "email": "deepak.kodihalli.83@gmail.com",
                        "username": "dkodihal"
                    },
                    "message": "This can also be done by users by introspecting the objects under the logging manager, right? Why do we need this API then?"
                },
                {
                    "file": "yaml/xyz/openbmc_project/Logging/Manager.interface.yaml",
                    "line": 3,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Amithash Prasad",
                        "email": "amithash@meta.com",
                        "username": "amithash"
                    },
                    "message": "It can get really expensive, especially if there are a lot of log entries."
                },
                {
                    "file": "yaml/xyz/openbmc_project/Logging/Manager.interface.yaml",
                    "line": 22,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Deepak Kodihalli",
                        "email": "deepak.kodihalli.83@gmail.com",
                        "username": "dkodihal"
                    },
                    "message": "Would we want to pass an array of these as tuples?"
                },
                {
                    "file": "yaml/xyz/openbmc_project/Logging/Manager.interface.yaml",
                    "line": 22,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Amithash Prasad",
                        "email": "amithash@meta.com",
                        "username": "amithash"
                    },
                    "message": "I did not need it in my case, but I can see if someone wants CALLOUT_INVENTORY_PATH/CALLOUT_DEVICE_PATH etc it might be useful. Do you envision such a case?"
                },
                {
                    "file": "yaml/xyz/openbmc_project/Logging/Manager.interface.yaml",
                    "line": 37,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Deepak Kodihalli",
                        "email": "deepak.kodihalli.83@gmail.com",
                        "username": "dkodihal"
                    },
                    "message": "Would the caller need to make more D-Bus calls to get further information related to these log objects?"
                },
                {
                    "file": "yaml/xyz/openbmc_project/Logging/Manager.interface.yaml",
                    "line": 37,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Amithash Prasad",
                        "email": "amithash@meta.com",
                        "username": "amithash"
                    },
                    "message": "Hopefully not. I am expecting the caller needs only a few. The primary use case was for search hint which associates a threshold event log to a unique hint. So, in that case we expect only one. But I can see things like, CALLOUT_INVENTORY_PATH etc, where we would need to go through all of them. In that case, yes, if the user is expecting more than a few to just go through all the object paths exposed by the service rather than try to optimize the number of calls."
                }
            ],
